  "settingsSectionDeclaration": "Software declaration",
  "settingsDeclineText": "This software (ArchoeraMusic) is open source under AGPL-3.0: you may freely use, study, modify and redistribute it, and comply-compliant commercial use is permitted; we do not offer closed-source commercial licensing outside AGPL obligations. Please read the following before use:\n\n",
  "settingsDecline1Title": "1. Software nature\n",
  "settingsDecline1Body": "This software is a third-party open-source client, not affiliated with, authorized by, or cooperating with any music platform or its official client. The project itself is not run for profit and accepts no commercial partnerships, ads or donations (commercial use of the code remains governed by AGPL-3.0). For richer features, please use the official client.\n\n",
  "settingsDeclineLicenseTitle": "2. Open-source license & source code\n",
  "settingsDeclineLicenseBody": "This software is released under the GNU Affero General Public License v3 (AGPL-3.0). Within the scope of that license, you are free to run, study, modify and redistribute this software, provided that you: retain the copyright and license notices; release your derivative works under the same license; and, if you make the functionality of this software (including modified versions) available to users over a network, provide those users with the corresponding complete source code. This project offers no closed-source commercial licensing outside AGPL obligations. The complete terms are governed by the accompanying LICENSE file and https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html.\n\n",
  "settingsDecline2Title": "2. Content sources & copyright\n",
  "settingsDecline2Body": "This software does not provide, store or distribute any music content itself. Audio, lyrics and covers come from your local files or public APIs of music platforms; copyright belongs to original rights holders and platforms. This software claims no ownership.\n\n",
  "settingsDecline3Title": "3. Copyright data processing obligations\n",
  "settingsDecline3Body": "Copyright data (playback URLs, lyrics, covers) generated during use is for your personal preview and research only; do not use for commercial or public distribution. It is recommended to clear within 24 hours. For long-term enjoyment, please purchase or subscribe through official channels to support legitimate music.\n\n",
  "settingsDecline4Title": "4. Usage restrictions\n",
  "settingsDecline4Body": "Do not use this software for commercial activities, bulk scraping, crawling or resale; do not use in violation of local laws or platform terms of service; do not bypass technical protection measures, access controls or terms of service of online platforms.\n\n",
  "settingsDeclineLoginTitle": "5. Login & account\n",
  "settingsDeclineLoginBody": "This software offers QR-code login (scan the QR code shown by this software with the platform''s official app) and credential login, to sync favorites and playlists and unlock related features. Please note:\n- The QR code is generated by the corresponding platform''s official API; this software does not collect, parse or send your login QR code, account, password or SMS verification code to any third party;\n- Session credentials obtained after login (cookies / tokens, etc.) are stored only on your device (encrypted in the credential vault) and are never uploaded to the developer or any non-platform server;\n- QR login means you authorize this software to access the platform with your account; actions such as favoriting, playing and commenting will genuinely affect your account;\n- Keep your device and system account secure; after logging in on a public or shared device, log out and clear credentials promptly;\n- The platform may apply risk control, restrictions or bans to third-party client logins; any account anomalies or restricted features arising from this are borne by you.\n\n",
  "settingsDeclineThirdPartyTitle": "7. Third-party services & risks\n",
  "settingsDeclineThirdPartyBody": "The APIs, authentication methods and availability of online music platforms are determined solely by the platforms and may change, be restricted or shut down at any time, causing login failures, unavailable features or unsynced data; this software is provided as is and makes no commitment regarding the continued availability, stability or data integrity of third-party services.\n\n",
  "settingsDeclineMinorTitle": "8. Use by minors\n",
  "settingsDeclineMinorBody": "This software is a general-purpose tool and is not designed for minors, nor does it collect personal information from them. If you are a minor, please read this declaration under the accompaniment and guidance of a guardian, obtain their consent, and then use this software; please also schedule your time sensibly and avoid unhealthy dependency.\n\n",
  "settingsDecline5Title": "8. Disclaimer\n",
  "settingsDecline5Body": "This software is provided \"as is\" without any express or implied warranties. Any direct or indirect losses arising from use or inability to use, or from API changes, account restrictions, expired login credentials, account risk control or bans, feature failures of online platforms shall be borne by the user.\n\n",
  "settingsDeclineFooter": "This software is for technical exploration and research only. If any platform finds this software inappropriate, please contact the developer for adjustment or removal.",
  "settingsDeclarationEntryDesc": "Nature, open-source license, restrictions & disclaimers",
  "settingsSectionLegal": "Legal & notices",
  "settingsLegalIntro": "Please read before use:",
  "settingsSectionPrivacy": "Privacy policy",
  "settingsPrivacyEntryDesc": "How we handle and protect your information",
  "settingsPrivacyIntro": "Welcome to ArchoeraMusic (the “Software” or “we”). We understand the importance of your personal information and are always committed to protecting your privacy and data security. This policy explains how we handle, store and protect your information during your use of the Software, and the rights you enjoy.\n\nPlease read and fully understand this policy carefully. By starting to use the Software, you confirm that you have read, understood and agreed to all of its contents.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy1Title": "1. Basic principles\n",
  "settingsPrivacy1Body": "1. Minimal necessity: we process only the data necessary to provide core features, ensure security and improve the experience, and do not collect personal sensitive information unrelated to the service.\n2. Local first: your library metadata, playback history and preferences are stored on your device by default and remain fully under your control.\n3. Transparent & controllable: this software contains no ads, tracking or user profiling; data processing is open and transparent and can be cleared by you at any time.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy2Title": "2. Information we process\n",
  "settingsPrivacy2Body": "· Information you provide: credentials for third-party music platforms (cookies / tokens obtained via QR login, account and password, etc.), the address and account of self-hosted or authorized media servers such as Subsonic, and the local music directories you select. Credentials are encrypted and stored in the local “credential vault” (v1 system secure storage / v2 passphrase protection / v3 device binding) and are never uploaded to the developer or any non-platform server.\n· Local runtime and cache data: library metadata (track names, artists, albums, etc.), playback history, favorites, download records, lyrics and cover caches, and preferences such as interface language and theme.\n· Local runtime logs: to help troubleshoot, the software generates runtime logs on your device (single-file cap 4 MiB, truncated in place once exceeded). Logs are kept only on your device and are never uploaded automatically unless you actively extract and provide them to the developer.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy3Title": "3. Purposes of use\n",
  "settingsPrivacy3Body": "We process the above information only for the following purposes: to provide core features such as music decoding, playback, lyrics display and the control interface; to restore your personal settings after you restart the software; and to ensure the software runs safely and stably on your device. We will never use your data for advertising, user profiling or commercial marketing, nor will we ever sell or rent it to any third party.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy4Title": "4. Third-party services\n",
  "settingsPrivacy4Body": "· Online music platforms and experimental sources: when you log in or use related features, requests are sent directly from your device to the corresponding platform (or interoperate through its public HTTP APIs), and the processing of related data is also governed by that platform’s own terms of service and privacy policy.\n· Self-hosted or personal media servers: communication with servers such as Subsonic takes place directly between your client and your server; data security and privacy on the server side are your and the server operator’s responsibility.\n· This software makes no commitment regarding the continued availability, stability or data handling practices of third-party services.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy5Title": "5. Storage, retention & security\n",
  "settingsPrivacy5Body": "The vast majority of your data is stored in the local data directory (Linux: ~/.local/share/ArchoeraMusic; macOS: ~/Library/Application Support/ArchoeraMusic; Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\ArchoeraMusic, overridable via the ARCHOERA_DATA_DIR environment variable) until you clear or delete it yourself. Sensitive credentials are encrypted using the operating system’s native secure storage where possible and isolated within the credential vault; network transmission uses HTTPS / TLS whenever the target supports it.\nAlthough we take reasonable security measures, inherent limitations of computing and storage technology mean no system can guarantee absolute 100% security; please keep your device and third-party account credentials safe.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy6Title": "6. Your rights & data management\n",
  "settingsPrivacy6Body": "You can view and modify preferences, streaming server information and login status in Settings at any time; you can clear caches, history and specified data under Storage / Security / History; you can view the local data directory in Settings and delete it yourself, or manually clean it up after uninstalling, to permanently destroy all data this software has left on your device. Please note: uninstalling the executable does not necessarily delete the data directory automatically.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy7Title": "7. Privacy of minors\n",
  "settingsPrivacy7Body": "This software is a general-purpose tool and does not collect any personal information from minors. If you are a minor, please read this policy under the accompaniment and guidance of a guardian and use this software after obtaining their consent.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy8Title": "8. Updates to this policy\n",
  "settingsPrivacy8Body": "We may revise this policy from time to time as features evolve, the technical architecture changes or laws and regulations are updated. Updated versions are released with the software or in the official repository and take effect from the “last updated” date shown at the top; if you continue to use the software after an update, you are deemed to have read, understood and agreed to the updated policy.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacy9Title": "9. Contact us\n",
  "settingsPrivacy9Body": "If you have any questions, comments or complaints about this policy, your information security or related matters, you are welcome to contact the developer at:\n· GitHub repository & Issues: https://github.com/BetaStudio2/ArchoeraMusic\nWe will reply as soon as possible after receiving your feedback.\n\n",
  "settingsPrivacyFooter": "This policy was last updated on September 29, 2026.",
